{"advance_requested_at_utc":"2026-10-11T12:11:09.135810+00:00","confirmed_proved":true,"job_id":"3d376b10-18aa-4b59-9ea0-2dec3650a0eb","last_publish_verdict":{"body":{"created_at":"2026-10-11T12:11:11.555754+00:00","definitions":"import Mathlib\n\nnamespace OAI\n\nopen scoped BigOperators\n\nnamespace PiExponent.InterpolationMatrix\n\n","error_message":"","formal_statement":"theorem exists_full_row_minor_of_surjective\r\n    {R C K : Type*} [Fintype R] [Fintype C] [DecidableEq R] [Field K]\r\n    (A : Matrix R C K) (hA : Function.Surjective A.mulVecLin) :\r\n    ∃ selection : R → C, Function.Injective selection ∧\r\n      (A.submatrix id selection).det ≠ 0 := by\n  sorry\n\nend PiExponent.InterpolationMatrix\n\nend OAI\n","id":"3d376b10-18aa-4b59-9ea0-2dec3650a0eb","kind":"problem","natural_language_statement":"Let $R$ and $C$ be finite index types, let $K$ be a field, and let $A=(A_{r,c})_{r\\in R,\\,c\\in C}$ be an $R$-by-$C$ matrix over $K$. Assume equality on $R$ is decidable and multiplication by $A$ defines a surjective $K$-linear map $K^C\\to K^R$. Then there is a function $s:R\\to C$ such that $s$ is injective and\n\n$$\n\\det\\bigl(A[\\operatorname{id}_R,s]\\bigr)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nThus the selected columns form a nonsingular square minor containing every row. This generic matrix-rank lemma is a direct core dependency for choosing a nonvanishing interpolation minor in the $\\pi$ irrationality-measure argument.","source":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/NumberTheory/PiExponent/Approximation/InterpolationMatrix.lean#L135-L166","status":"PUBLISHED","tags":["linear-algebra","matrix-theory","openai-pi-exponent-017"],"theorem_id":"f3ace940-1663-489e-af28-d1f63c803801","theorem_name":"OAI.PiExponent.InterpolationMatrix.exists_full_row_minor_of_surjective","theorem_title":"A surjective matrix has a nonsingular full-row minor","updated_at":"2026-10-11T12:11:21.655564+00:00","visibility":"public"},"http_status":200},"